# SYNTHETIC DEMO SESSION for tools/dashboard.py - mixed file, NOT a measurement.
#
# Part 1 (up to the '# ---- SYNTHETIC from here' line) is REAL: the third Step 10 boot
# captured from the ESP32-C5 on COM13 on 2026-09-25 (laptop hotspot 'Testing', channel 1,
# L-LTF 106 B / 26 subcarriers). Line text verbatim; timestamps shifted by -48.28 s so the
# file starts at 0. 'port open' is the capture tool's own note, not the board.
#
# Everything after that line is SYNTHETIC: generated by a script. The EXPLAIN and 'why:' line
# formats follow step10's main.c (CSI_EXPLAIN) as written on 2026-09-25, which had not run on
# hardware yet, so they show the format, not captured output. Every number (distances,
# votes, breathing) is invented to be plausible. 'raj' and 'asha' are placeholder enrolled people; the third walker is an
# unenrolled colleague. The 4-per-second human-readable bar line is left out of the
# synthetic part to keep the file small.
#
# Format: "%7.2f <line>" (seconds, then the serial line) - what serial_capture.py and
# dashboard.py --log write. Lines starting with # are skipped by dashboard.py --replay.
#
#   python tools\dashboard.py --replay tools\sample_session.log --speed 4 --open
